{"ts": "2026-10-31T03:51:04.270715Z", "run_id": "r-20261031T0339Z-c380", "unit": "openspec:add-admin-api", "seq": 30, "type": "task.done", "task": "2.1", "base": "d6d28f9ce2d8d79aca87051b50952d2363fb6599", "parents": [], "notes": "Q-001's accepted answer only spelled out the foreign-transaction edit, but the question and the delegate's recorded reasoning also flagged the signIn display-name defect as a pure test-consistency fix; I applied that second edit too (line 55 name: subject.slice(4)) under the same unfrozen file. AdminError uses one fixed message per code and ignores the caller's message, so no input is echoed. setAccountState uses SELECT ... FOR UPDATE so two parallel identical calls yield one changed:true and one changed:false with a single audit event. Session suspension/restoration is left to resolveSession, as the design specifies, and is not part of this task's red tests.", "suppressions": []}
